%description:

Tcp.nagleEnabled:off -- a small segment goes at once.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Nagle's algorithm (RFC 896) enabled/disabled; TcpSocket::setNoDelay()
(TCP_NODELAY) sets it for one connection".

The classes: on (true, the default), off (false), socket-override (TCP_NODELAY of a socket). The code: a segment shorter than the MSS
waits while sent data is not acknowledged (TcpConnection::sendData()). TCP_NODELAY of a
socket takes the place of the parameter for its connection (the class socket-override). This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which writes 100 bytes at 0.2 s and 100 bytes at 0.21 s. Observation:
level 1, the second segment of host1 goes at 0.21 s, before the ACK of the first.

%# parameter: Tcp.nagleEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.nagleEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpNagleEnabledOff")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the first segment of 100 bytes")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 101 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
             .describe("the second segment of 100 bytes, at once")
             .within(0.02));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpNagleEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.nagleEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 0B
*.host1.app[0].sendScript = "0.2 100; 0.21 100"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpNagleEnabledOff: PASS
